module test.claim.product.p4261_enable_chain_sheet_witness

// ==================================================================================================
// Sheet 2, U1_P5's enable and the Q300 / Q301 pair, held to what a partial schematic built from
// readings may claim.
//
//   * Every connection cites the E1-b's readings between exactly its two points and is admissible; every
//     one is a reported zero, so none joins and each node's only member is its anchor.
//   * P6 is pin 7's node by the operator's ruling: the sheet draws the ruling as a continuation and no
//     node reaches both.
//   * The kilohm readings from Q300's lead b are links, each citing its readings, and a link citing a
//     reading between other points is refused. A link read both ways round keeps its direction: the
//     report gives every reading's range and red-probe point, and the drawing names the red probe's
//     point on such a link.
//   * Lead roles are candidates on physical leads, and an identical correspondence that names two
//     different terminals is refused.
//   * The hypothesis is the investigation's own, cited once, with candidates beyond the sheet.
//   * Every read names a target the sheet carries and at least two outcomes.
//   * Membership is what is reachable from the anchor over copper edges: an isolated joined pair, or a joined
//     tail behind a proposed bridge, is not a member; admitting the bridge makes the chain reachable.
//   * Two pads of one footprint tied by evidenced external copper join; sharing a component identity is
//     not a refusal.
//   * The sheet is drawn in one declared E1-b state: a later reading of the same pair, or a later voltage at
//     the same point, is refused and never enters this state's view.
//   * The sheet exports, and the drawing carries the ruling, the roles and the measurement table.
// ==================================================================================================
